          "normalized_summary": "Pesticide exposure during childhood may quietly shift one of puberty’s most important milestones. Researchers in Spain found that exposure to two common pesticide-related compounds was associated with changes in the timing of menstruation. One was linked to an earlier first period, while the other was connected to a later one. The findings suggest that chemicals [...]",
