          "normalized_title": "New Treatment Targets Gum Disease Without Killing Good Bacteria",
          "normalized_summary": "A targeted light-activated therapy may treat periodontitis without disrupting the beneficial bacteria that help maintain oral health. Treating periodontitis presents a difficult balance: harmful bacteria need to be removed without wiping out the beneficial microbes that help maintain a healthy mouth. Researchers at Nagoya University in Japan have developed an experimental approach designed to do [...]",
